<http://data.silknow.org/object/2d135d6e-fc9c-3f3c-a94f-1865db276f6c>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "For a girl: silver grey satin, hand quilted and trimmed with fringed edging, English, 1845-1850"@en , "The body of this baby's bonnet's exterior is a silver, quilted, Japanese silk satin with box pleated, frayed silk trim. The bonnet's brim has a wire edge to preserve its shape. There is a silk curtain attached at the bonnet's base which would have covered child's neck, suggesting that this is a girl's bonnet. Two blue ribbons are attached to the side of the bonnet to tie it under the child's chin. Inside the bonnet, there is a wadded duck egg blue silk brim. Holland linen was used at the crown and the whole hat is constructed in buckram."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/fd81119a-39cc-3fc4-913b-76229ad90946> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/459d7c3d-7738-3fa4-b39c-31252d4bb839> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "For a girl: silver grey satin, hand quilted and trimmed with fringed edging, English, 1845-1850"@en , "The body of this baby's bonnet's exterior is a silver, quilted, Japanese silk satin with box pleated, frayed silk trim. The bonnet's brim has a wire edge to preserve its shape. There is a silk curtain attached at the bonnet's base which would have covered child's neck, suggesting that this is a girl's bonnet. Two blue ribbons are attached to the side of the bonnet to tie it under the child's chin. Inside the bonnet, there is a wadded duck egg blue silk brim. Holland linen was used at the crown and the whole hat is constructed in buckram."@en ;
